{"id":"p19-l07","minutes":30,"summary":"An N-channel high-side MOSFET needs a gate voltage above its own source, which floats at the input voltage. You learn how gate drivers and bootstrap circuits provide it, size a bootstrap capacitor from the charge it must deliver, simulate its charge and droop cycle by cycle, and see why a bootstrap cannot hold the switch on at 100 % duty.","html":"<h2 id=\"why-a-driver\">Why a driver</h2>\n<p>A MOSFET switches when its gate-source capacitance is charged to about 10 V and discharged to 0 V. Charging <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> in 20 ns needs <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">60</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">nC</span></span><span class=\"mord\">/20</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">ns</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span></span> A of peak current, far more than a microcontroller pin gives. A <strong>gate driver</strong> amplifies the logic signal into amperes of gate current, adds dead time between the high and low switches, and often an undervoltage lockout (UVLO) that keeps the switches off when the gate supply is too low to turn them fully on.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-high-side-problem\">The high-side problem</h2>\n<p>In a half-bridge (buck, motor inverter) the high-side N-channel MOSFET’s source is the switch node, which swings between 0 V and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">in</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. To turn it on, its gate must be about 10 V <em>above</em> <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">in</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. A <strong>bootstrap</strong> circuit makes this supply: a diode and capacitor <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> from the driver’s 12 V supply to the switch node.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Low side on: the switch node is at ground, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> charges to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">dd</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.1076em;\">f</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> through the diode.</li>\n<li>High side on: the switch node rises to <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">in</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, carrying <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> with it. The diode blocks, and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> powers the floating high-side driver.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"sizing\">Sizing</h2>\n<p>While the high side is on, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> supplies the gate charge, the floating driver’s quiescent current, leakage and level-shifter charge. For a droop of at most <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span></span>:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:2.113em;vertical-align:-0.686em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen nulldelimiter\"></span><span class=\"mfrac\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.427em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.314em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">Δ</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.23em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"frac-line\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.677em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">ak</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">t</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">o</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">n</span><span class=\"mpunct mtight\">,</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">ma</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.686em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose nulldelimiter\"></span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Choose a value several times larger, with a low-ESR ceramic capacitor rated above <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">dd</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>. The capacitor recharges only while the low side is on, so the duty cycle cannot reach 100 % for long: the voltage drains towards the UVLO threshold. Designs that need 100 % duty use a charge pump or an isolated supply.</p>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"bootstrap\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Bootstrap capacitor voltage over switching cycles: charging when the low side is on, drooping when the high side is on. Change the capacitor, duty cycle and gate charge.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>Illustrative values: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">g</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">60</span></span></span></span> nC, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8778em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">Q</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">s</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span> nC, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">150</span></span></span></span> µA, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0197em;\">l</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">e</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">ak</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">20</span></span></span></span> µA, 20 kHz at <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">D</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.9</span></span></span></span> (on-time 45 µs), 12 V driver supply, 0.6 V diode:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The charge per cycle is 72.7 nC, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">145</span></span></span></span> nF for 0.5 V droop. We choose 470 nF.</li>\n<li>The simulation starts at 11.4 V and its minimum is 11.226 V, a droop of 0.174 V, within the 0.5 V budget.</li>\n<li>At 100 % duty the voltage reaches the 8 V undervoltage lockout after 9.02 ms and the driver turns the switch off.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">bootstrap.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">boot_cap</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">qg=<span class=\"hljs-number\">60e-9</span>, iq=<span class=\"hljs-number\">150e-6</span>, ileak=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20e-6</span>, t_on=<span class=\"hljs-number\">50e-6</span>, dv=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>, qls=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-9</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;bootstrap capacitor: it must deliver the gate charge, the high-side driver&#x27;s quiescent and leakage current\n    for the longest on-time, and the level-shifter charge, while drooping no more than dv&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    q = qg + (iq + ileak) * t_on + qls; <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> q / dv, q\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">simulate</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">Cb, vdd=<span class=\"hljs-number\">12.0</span>, vf=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>, r_chg=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5.0</span>, qg=<span class=\"hljs-number\">60e-9</span>, iq=<span class=\"hljs-number\">150e-6</span>, ileak=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20e-6</span>, qls=<span class=\"hljs-number\">5e-9</span>, fs=<span class=\"hljs-number\">20e3</span>, D=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span>, periods=<span class=\"hljs-number\">200</span>, n=<span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span></span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;&quot;&quot;switch-node cycles: low side on -&gt; Cb charges from Vdd through the diode and a resistance;\n    high side on -&gt; Cb supplies the gate charge at turn-on, then the driver&#x27;s quiescent and leakage current&quot;&quot;&quot;</span>\n    T = <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> / fs; dt = T / n; v = vdd - vf; hist, vmin, was_on = [], v, <span class=\"hljs-literal\">False</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> p <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(periods):\n        <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> k <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(n):\n            on = k &lt; <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(D * n)\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> on:                                                            <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># high side on: switch node at Vin</span>\n                <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">not</span> was_on: v -= (qg + qls) / Cb                           <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># gate charge pulled at turn-on</span>\n                v -= (iq + ileak) * dt / Cb\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">else</span>:                                                             <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># low side on: switch node at ground</span>\n                v += <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, (vdd - vf - v) / r_chg) * dt / Cb\n            was_on = on\n            v = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(v, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>); vmin = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">min</span>(vmin, v)\n            <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> p == periods - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">or</span> D &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>: hist.append(v)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> vmin, np.array(hist)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_sizing_and_droop</span>():\n    t_on = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.9</span> / <span class=\"hljs-number\">20e3</span>; Cb, q = boot_cap(t_on=t_on)\n    C_pick = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.47e-6</span>                                                          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># next standard value above, with margin</span>\n    vmin, _ = simulate(C_pick)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;charge per cycle <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e9</span> * q:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> nC -&gt; Cb &gt;= <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">1e9</span> * Cb:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.0</span>f}</span> nF for 0.5 V droop; chosen 470 nF&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;simulated minimum bootstrap voltage <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{vmin:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> V (start <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span>:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> V), droop <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span> - vmin:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.3</span>f}</span> V&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> C_pick &gt;= Cb <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> <span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.6</span> - vmin &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">test_hundred_percent_duty</span>():\n    _, h = simulate(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.47e-6</span>, D=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.0</span>, periods=<span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span>)                              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># 20 ms with the high side always on</span>\n    uvlo = <span class=\"hljs-number\">8.0</span>; t_fail = np.argmax(h &lt; uvlo) * (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> / <span class=\"hljs-number\">20e3</span> / <span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;100 % duty: the bootstrap voltage reaches the <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{uvlo}</span> V undervoltage lockout after <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{<span class=\"hljs-number\">1000</span> * t_fail:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> ms&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> (h &lt; uvlo).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">any</span>() <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> t_fail &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">20e-3</span>                                <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># a bootstrap cannot hold the gate on forever</span>\n\ntest_sizing_and_droop()\ntest_hundred_percent_duty()\n<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;PASS&quot;</span>)</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"in-practice\">In practice</h2>\n<p>Half-bridge drivers such as the IR2110 family, the TI UCC27211 or the gate drivers integrated in motor-driver chips have bootstrap diodes inside or need an external fast diode. Their datasheets give <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.9694em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0785em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">q</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> and the formula above. In ngspice, simulate a few hundred cycles to check the droop and the start-up, when <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> is empty and needs a few low-side pulses before the high side can switch.</p>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>At start-up the bootstrap capacitor is empty. What must the controller do before the first high-side pulse?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>Turn the low side on (or run a few short low-side pulses) so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> charges through the diode. Many drivers hold the high side off until the bootstrap voltage passes its UVLO.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why is the bootstrap diode a fast or ultrafast type?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>When the switch node rises, the diode must block quickly. A slow diode conducts in reverse during recovery, discharging <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3361em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0715em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">b</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> into the supply and causing losses and noise.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p19-l07\"></div>\n","toc":[{"id":"why-a-driver","title":"Why a driver"},{"id":"the-high-side-problem","title":"The high-side problem"},{"id":"sizing","title":"Sizing"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"in-practice","title":"In practice"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p19-l07-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Minimum bootstrap capacitor for 80 nC per cycle and 0.4 V droop (nF)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Q/ΔV.</p>\n","answer":200,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l07-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Charge drawn by 200 µA over a 100 µs on-time (nC)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>I t.</p>\n","answer":20,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l07-q3","type":"num","q":"<p>Peak gate current to deliver 40 nC in 10 ns (A)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Q/t.</p>\n","answer":4,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l07-q4","type":"num","q":"<p>Initial bootstrap voltage from a 15 V supply with a 0.7 V diode (V)?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Vdd − Vf.</p>\n","answer":14.3,"tol":0.002,"unit":""},{"id":"p19-l07-q5","type":"mc","q":"<p>The bootstrap capacitor recharges when…</p>\n","explain":"<p>Only then is the diode forward biased.</p>\n","options":["the low-side switch is on and the switch node is at ground","the input voltage is maximum","both switches are on","the high-side switch is on"],"answer":0},{"id":"p19-l07-q6","type":"mc","q":"<p>A design that must keep the high-side switch on indefinitely needs…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A bootstrap only refills during low-side on-time.</p>\n","options":["a lower switching frequency","a charge pump or isolated gate supply","a slower diode","a larger bootstrap capacitor only"],"answer":1}],"code":[{"file":"bootstrap.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\ndef boot_cap(qg=60e-9, iq=150e-6, ileak=20e-6, t_on=50e-6, dv=0.5, qls=5e-9):\n    \"\"\"bootstrap capacitor: it must deliver the gate charge, the high-side driver's quiescent and leakage current\n    for the longest on-time, and the level-shifter charge, while drooping no more than dv\"\"\"\n    q = qg + (iq + ileak) * t_on + qls; return q / dv, q\n\ndef simulate(Cb, vdd=12.0, vf=0.6, r_chg=5.0, qg=60e-9, iq=150e-6, ileak=20e-6, qls=5e-9, fs=20e3, D=0.9, periods=200, n=400):\n    \"\"\"switch-node cycles: low side on -> Cb charges from Vdd through the diode and a resistance;\n    high side on -> Cb supplies the gate charge at turn-on, then the driver's quiescent and leakage current\"\"\"\n    T = 1 / fs; dt = T / n; v = vdd - vf; hist, vmin, was_on = [], v, False\n    for p in range(periods):\n        for k in range(n):\n            on = k < round(D * n)\n            if on:                                                            # high side on: switch node at Vin\n                if not was_on: v -= (qg + qls) / Cb                           # gate charge pulled at turn-on\n                v -= (iq + ileak) * dt / Cb\n            else:                                                             # low side on: switch node at ground\n                v += max(0.0, (vdd - vf - v) / r_chg) * dt / Cb\n            was_on = on\n            v = max(v, 0.0); vmin = min(vmin, v)\n            if p == periods - 1 or D >= 1: hist.append(v)\n    return vmin, np.array(hist)\n\ndef test_sizing_and_droop():\n    t_on = 0.9 / 20e3; Cb, q = boot_cap(t_on=t_on)\n    C_pick = 0.47e-6                                                          # next standard value above, with margin\n    vmin, _ = simulate(C_pick)\n    print(f\"charge per cycle {1e9 * q:.1f} nC -> Cb >= {1e9 * Cb:.0f} nF for 0.5 V droop; chosen 470 nF\")\n    print(f\"simulated minimum bootstrap voltage {vmin:.3f} V (start {12 - 0.6:.1f} V), droop {12 - 0.6 - vmin:.3f} V\")\n    assert C_pick >= Cb and 12 - 0.6 - vmin < 0.5\n\ndef test_hundred_percent_duty():\n    _, h = simulate(0.47e-6, D=1.0, periods=400)                              # 20 ms with the high side always on\n    uvlo = 8.0; t_fail = np.argmax(h < uvlo) * (1 / 20e3 / 400)\n    print(f\"100 % duty: the bootstrap voltage reaches the {uvlo} V undervoltage lockout after {1000 * t_fail:.2f} ms\")\n    assert (h < uvlo).any() and t_fail < 20e-3                                # a bootstrap cannot hold the gate on forever\n\ntest_sizing_and_droop()\ntest_hundred_percent_duty()\nprint(\"PASS\")"}]}